what's the real story behind aunt viv  being replaced on the fresh prince which  cast member on frasier was the biggest  prima donna  behind all the smiles and life lessons  tv families often have as much drama as  real families  it wasn't all lovely ladies with golden  curls on the set of the brady bunch  especially when maureen mccormick and  eve plum were shooting together as  sisters marsha and jan respectively well  all i hear all day long at school is how  great marsha is at this or how wonderful  marsha did that marsha marsha marsha  as mccormick revealed in her 2009 memoir  here's the story plum resented her for  quote getting too much attention and it  only became worse as the kids grew up  susan olsen who played youngest brady's  sister cindy told fox news in 2009 that  mccormick and plum were eventually no  longer on speaking terms to the point  that whenever we get together for any  project there will only be one or the  other as olsen further explained eve got  tired of maureen gaining attention for  herself by regurgitating the tiresome  and false insinuations that they had a  lesbian affair fortunately like most  brady stories this one ultimately has a  happy ending as the on-screen sisters  had a chance to settle their squabble in  the hgtv miniseries a very brady  renovation which premiered in 2019 as  plum admitted to e it had been a really  long time since we had all been together  and it's really cool to see who people  are today and what they're doing it's  awesome it's so nice to reconnect with  people that you care about  who can forget the public spectacle that  was charlie sheen's exit from two and a  half men it should come as no surprise  that his fire burned a few bridges along  the way  the exact timeline of his departure from  the show is unclear but it undeniably  reached ahead when he called creator  chuck laurie a clown and a turd while  calling into alex jones's radio show  shortly afterwards sheen was fired from  the sitcom and the punches didn't stop  there after his firing sheen went on to  tell e news that his on-screen brother  john cryer was quote a turn coat a  traitor and a troll crier apparently  hadn't been outspoken enough in favor of  sheen after his firing and sheen also  claimed that he hadn't reached out to  him although crier claimed otherwise but  it seems that there are no hard feelings  too tough to forgive among tv families  as laurie later told entertainment  tonight that he didn't feel like he and  sheen were ever in a feud  i felt like he was my friend  i really loved the guy  crier meanwhile had more mixed feelings  about his time with sheen as he put it  in his memoir so that happened to some  sheen was a rebel a truth-teller willing  to poke his masters in the eye of course  charlie wasn't those things he was  simply lashing out at the people who  told him the party was over  the wb series charmed was anything but  at least not behind the scenes if  anything this late 90s early 2000s drama  about three magical sisters was rather  cursed shannon doherty and alyssa milano  played two of the sisters and they grew  to have a real-life beef so big that it  led to doherty's departure from the show  as milano recounted to e news in 2020  there were times when i'd come in and  say good morning shannon and she didn't  say anything to me and there were times  when she'd come in and say good morning  alyssa and i wouldn't say anything to  her  for doherty the routine silent  treatments weren't worth the paycheck as  she told entertainment tonight in 2001  i'm 30 years old and i don't have time  for drama in my life anymore with any  family infighting time passes people  grow there are regrets and hopefully  there are amends as milano later  admitted to entertainment tonight in  2021 i can take responsibility for a lot  of our attention  likewise doherty is letting bygones be  bygones as she put it on a 2015  appearance on sway in the morning are  there times that were rough yeah i mean  i think that when you work that closely  together there's always going to be  times that are rough sometimes you don't  always get along with the person  24 7 that you work with  while steve urkel technically had no  blood relation to the winslow family on  family matters he was at their house so  often that he deserves an honorary spot  at the table and the irate responses to  him from the winslow's on the show may  not have been too far from what was  going on behind the scenes on a 2021  episode of tv one's uncensored urkel  actor jaleel white rehashed some of the  early tension between himself and the  older actors on the show  as he put it i was not welcome to the  cast at all they know what it was i  didn't think anything of it being cast  to be on family matters because it was  supposed to only be a guest spot one and  done  as the story goes the other actors  bristled when the network shifted much  of the show's focus over to urkel as  reported by entertainment weekly there  was one particularly notable occasion  that also involved reginald valjohnson  and joe marie payton who played the  winslow parents white had to put on a  dress and two older actors pressured him  against wearing it as white recalled  they were very sensitive to putting  black men in dresses but over time the  familiarity among the cast improved  according to white phil johnson and  peyton do deserve credit at times for  having helped foster a more harmonious  environment  and we did become very much a family  isn't that the best any family real or  fictitious can help for  on the fresh prince of bel air aunt  vivian may have had the run of the  mansion but behind the scenes well smith  was definitely the top dog viewers may  recall the jarring recasting of aunt viv  originally played by janet hubert who  was replaced by daphne maxwell reed in  the fourth season and it wasn't exactly  a smooth transition for the rest of the  cast in a 2020 interview on wabc's here  and now hubert discussed her departure  from fresh prince she explained that she  wasn't fired but rather that she  rejected her contract renewal in the  hopes that the network would return with  a better offer instead they replaced her  though she wasn't surprised in her eyes  the production team seemed to have it  out for her as she put it they told me i  had to go into my dressing room in  between takes because i wasn't laughing  at will's jokes she even went so far as  to claim  the cast was offered money to take me  down hubert had a chance to confront  smith on a fresh prince reunion that  aired on hbo max in 2020. she didn't  hold back i've been banished  and they said it was you who  who banished me  he then offered an apology he reflected  further on the experience during the red  table talk interview as he admitted that  he was shaking during their conversation  that's not  who i want to be  and it's not  how i want to make people feel  hopefully smith makes the most of this  second chance  the jackson brothers on the nbc sitcom  were known for their bickering just like  any siblings who ultimately loved each  other but behind the scenes it was a  little more violent as todd bridges  reportedly slapped gary coleman although  coleman reportedly cast the first palm  bridges who played older brother willis  recounted the story of this backstage  fight in his 2010 autobiography killing  willis bridges felt that coleman was  getting too egotistical as his character  arnold was gaining popularity among the  fans according to bridges coleman would  always have an obnoxious comeback to  everything that was said around the set  on one occasion when he couldn't come up  with a comeback he slapped bridges who  then slapped him back unlike some of the  feuds on this list this one sadly does  not have the chance for a reconciliation  each of the three young leads bridges  coleman and dana plato struggled with  their fame after the show's conclusion  plato died of an overdose in 1999 while  coleman passed away in 2010 after  enduring financial struggles that led to  him declaring bankruptcy bridges who  dealt with his own drug addiction is now  the only surviving member of the  original main cast he's doing better  though as he put it during a 2016  appearance on the dr oz show i love life  now life is the best thing in the world  it's hard to forget roseanne barr's  explosive exit from the revival of her  eponymous abc sitcom in 2018 but just in  case you forgot here's a quick refresher  barr tweeted about former obama  administration advisor valerie jarrett  in which she linked her to the muslim  brotherhood and planet of the apes she  was then subsequently fired by abc for  the remark the rest of the cast narrowly  avoided a complete cancellation when  roseanne was rebranded as the spin-off  series the connors  in response to barr's tweet sarah  gilbert who plays roseanne's daughter  darlene tweeted in response  roseanne's recent comments about valerie  jarrett and so much more are abhorrent  and do not reflect the beliefs of our  cast and crew or anyone associated with  our show i am disappointed in her  actions to say the least  barr responded in turn as she claimed  that gilbert quote destroyed the show  and my life with that tweet despite this  rocky episode the connors has gone on to  flourish on abc and ultimately it would  seem that just like in real life some  family disputes are irreconcilable  for the most part the cast of frasier  appears to have been entirely amicable  with each other the human cast that is  as for family pup eddie he was actually  portrayed by two different canine actors  he was originally played by a jack  russell terrier named moose but he came  to share the role with his son enzo as  he got older often enough family and  business just don't mix and that was  certainly true on the set of frasier in  an interview on the show animal  magnetism enzo's trainer mathilde  ducanni revealed musa nanzo's  relationship is so bad that they can't  even be in the same room together  moose may be more to blame as decanny  explained that before he was an actor  his owners gave him up he had been  nothing else but a terror  the interviewers then connected the  bristling relationship between moose and  enzo to the equally difficult one  between human father and son duo frazier  and martin crane sadly enzo and moose  have both since passed now that their  on-set days are over hopefully they've  reconciled in doggy heaven  it's easy to over romanticize an iconic  classic sitcom like the andy griffith  show and certainly griffith himself  surely wanted audiences to have that  feeling as he put it in a 1996 today  show interview  it was of a time gone by but despite the  simple times in front of the camera  there was drama behind the scenes for  the most part the set of mayberry seems  to have been as blissful as the show  made it seem but one bit of trouble in  paradise stemmed from the difficult  relationship between griffith and his  cast mate frances bavier who played aunt  b  ron howard who played andy's son opie  discussed his memories of making the  show during an interview with the  television academy as he put it i don't  think she felt a part of what these boys  were up to in their shenanigans  while the cast has managed to keep  relatively tight lift about any  unpleasant feelings griffith did reveal  some details about his relationship with  bavier during an interview with ralph  emery on the show on the record  as he recalled she wasn't always in real  great shape emotionally but toward the  end of bavier's life griffith called her  and made amends as he recounted i hadn't  talked to her in a long time she said  i'm sorry we didn't get along better she  said it was my fault hopefully this  clearing of the air gave bavier some  degree of peace check out one of our  newest videos right here plus even more  looper videos about your favorite tv  shows are coming soon subscribe to our  youtube channel and hit the bell so you  don't miss a single one  [Music]  you

